<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!-- Call recording. The code is already compiled into the shipped Dialer
         (packages/apps/Dialer/java/com/android/dialer/callrecord/) and
         CAPTURE_AUDIO_OUTPUT is already on its privapp allowlist; upstream just
         ships the feature switched off. Both values are read through
         getResources() at callrecord/impl/CallRecorderService.java:86 and :220,
         so an overlay is all it takes.

         FLIPPING THIS ALONE WOULD DO NOTHING HERE. LineageOS gates the record
         button on a per-country allowlist as well, and the Netherlands is not
         on it. See the companion overlay of xml/call_record_states.xml. Both
         files are needed, and the owner asked for the feature explicitly.

         audio_source 4 is VOICE_CALL, which captures uplink AND downlink. It is
         not implemented on every MediaTek audio HAL and this one has not been
         tested. IF A TEST CALL RECORDS ONLY YOUR OWN SIDE, this is why: fall
         back to 1 (MIC), which on this chassis picks up the far end only
         through earpiece leakage and is usually not worth keeping. Treat the
         VOICE_CALL result as the go/no-go for the whole change. -->
    <bool name="call_recording_enabled">true</bool>
    <integer name="call_recording_audio_source">4</integer>
</resources>
